{"count": 26429, "next": "https://api.acmi.net.au/creators/?page=1229", "previous": "https://api.acmi.net.au/creators/?page=1227", "results": [{"id": 72724, "name": "Scott Redford", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2373483, "title": "Blood disco: Dirk wears white socks", "work_id": 109403, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1962", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "Born 1962, lives and works in Brisbane.\nRedford is an artist and curator. He has exhibited nationally since 1983 and internationally since 1997. In 2001-03 Redford was the recipient of an Australia Council Residency at the Kunstlerhaus Bethanien, Berlin. Major exhibitions he has participated in include the 1993 and 1999 Australian Perspectas at the Art Gallery of New South Wales; the 1996 Adelaide Biennale of Australian Art at Art Gallery of South Australia; Photographica Australis Taipei Art Museum, Taiwan and Asian tour; and Fieldwork: Australian Art 1968-2002, National Gallery of Victoria, 2002.", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2023-07-05T03:40:53.326868+10:00", "external_links": [], "uuid": "5aee2c93-d8b5-461a-966f-e1308fb81f22", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "2047", "external_references": [{"id": 52123, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q121361219"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-06T01:08:53.663099+10:00"}, {"id": 72723, "name": "Janet Merewether", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2373480, "title": "Knit-face", "work_id": 109402, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2318811, "title": "Surplus government asset", "work_id": 87642, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 2144180, "title": "Contemporary case studies", "work_id": 93043, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "Born lives and works in Sydney.\nMerewether is a film director and media artist who has studied at Sydney College of the Arts and Australian Film Television and Radio School, and is completing her master's at the University of Technology, Sydney. Her award-winning short films and videos have screened in numerous festivals internationally including the New York Film Festival. Her latest film, Short Before the Movie, premiered at the New Directors/New Films festival at MoMA, New York. She is currently developing a documentary entitled Jabe Babe: A Heightened Life and completing her short film Palermo: 'History' Standing Still. Retrospectives of her work have screened in Berlin, Boston, Seoul and Taipei.", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2023-07-05T03:40:52.006138+10:00", "external_links": [], "uuid": "895309fe-9428-4bf5-baae-08c49a6a1035", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "110733", "external_references": [{"id": 51152, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q121361144"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-05T21:08:32.801820+10:00"}, {"id": 72722, "name": "Simryn Gill", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2373468, "title": "Vessel", "work_id": 109398, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "1959", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "Born 1959 Singapore, lives and works in Sydney.\nGill currently divides her time between Sydney and Port Dickson, Malaysia. Her art practice involves object-making, compiling collections, photography and the use of text. Her recent solo exhibitions have been held at Ikon Gallery, Birmingham, England, 2000; Petronas Gallery, Kuala Lumpur, 2001; the Art Gallery of New South Wales, 2002; and the Berkeley Art Museum, University of California, 2004. She received an Australia Council Fellowship in 2003.", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2023-07-05T03:40:45.700908+10:00", "external_links": [], "uuid": "99100abd-1169-4780-978d-da3c6424018a", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "2042", "external_references": [{"id": 51535, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q121361069"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-06T01:21:03.011180+10:00"}, {"id": 72721, "name": "Vernon Ah Kee", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2373459, "title": "Whitefellanormal", "work_id": 109395, "role": "producer/director", "role_id": 31, "is_primary": true}], "also_known_as": "", "date_of_birth": "", "date_of_death": "", "genders": [], "languages": [], "places_of_operation": [], "biography": "Born in North Queensland, lives and works in Brisbane.\nAh Kee holds a Bachelor of Visual Arts in contemporary Australian Indigenous art and an honours in Fine Art; he is currently researching his doctorate. Ah Kee's work is primarily a critique of Australian popular culture, specifically the black/white dichotomy. Recently he has concentrated on a conceptual use of text and minimal expression, combining a combative writing style with a strong visual sense. He has exhibited in group and solo shows, and he currently lectures on contemporary Australian Indigenous art at Queensland College of Arts, with interests including Aboriginal education, identity and art.\nVernon Ah Kee is represented by Bellas Milani Gallery, Brisbane.", "biography_author": null, "date_of_biography": "2023-07-05T03:40:41.359136+10:00", "external_links": [], "uuid": "0e288f38-1c5f-41b5-84a9-38a43794e882", "source": {"name": "Vernon", "slug": "vernon"}, "source_identifier": "2054", "external_references": [{"id": 52224, "source": {"name": "Wikidata", "slug": "wikidata"}, "source_identifier": "Q121360790"}], "date_modified": "2023-09-06T02:03:38.974860+10:00"}, {"id": 72061, "name": "Kale Frost", "roles_in_work": [{"id": 2363019, "t